## Next Steps for the User
1. Create a **private** repository on GitHub.
2. Initialize git locally (Done): `git init`, `git add .`, `git commit -m "initial commit"`.
3. Link the remote: `git remote add origin https://github.com/allumnova/startupideaexchange.git`.
4. Push to main: (Done) `git push -u origin main`.
5. **CRITICAL**: Go to your repository **Settings** -> **Danger Zone** -> **Change visibility** -> Select **Private** to make it confidential.
6. Set up the GitHub Secrets listed above.
6. On the VPS, create the directory `~/startup-marketplace` and place the [docker-compose.prod.yml](file:///c:/my_projects/startupidea/docker-compose.prod.yml) file there (or let the script handle it if you refine the CI/CD).

